# Architecture Blueprint

## Tech Stack & Core Constraints
- Framework: Next.js (App Router)
- Language: TypeScript (Strict type safety, no 'any')
- Styling: Tailwind CSS (Utility-first, responsive design)
- Icons: Lucide React

## Folder Structure
All new features and elements must strictly adhere to this structure:
- `src/app/`: File-based routing, server components by default.
- `src/components/ui/`: Low-level, atomic, reusable layout primitives (e.g., buttons, inputs).
- `src/components/sections/`: High-level landing page components (e.g., Hero, Projects, Skills).
- `src/lib/`: Pure utility functions, state management, or static constants data.

## Development Principles
- Server Components by default. Only include `'use client'` when interactive state hooks (`useState`, `useEffect`) or browser event handlers are actively required.
- Maintain accessible, semantic HTML layout structure (`<main>`, `<section>`, `<nav>`, `<h1>-<h6>`).
- Do not install external visual dependencies without asking first. Use native Tailwind features where possible.